B) The first is a functional requirement (the specific behavior expected); the second is an  
   infrastructure/non-functional requirement (a performance and capacity constraint the  
   implementation must satisfy).
C) Both statements are infrastructure requirements, since both are ultimately implemented in  
   code running on infrastructure.
D) The first is a business goal, not a requirement at all, and only the second should be  
   documented.

