### Q2.14 · Claude Application Design
A team ships a plugin bundling a house-style writing skill and a set of internal commands,  
distributed to every developer's Claude Code setup via their plugin marketplace config.  
Three months later, a security review finds the plugin still requests filesystem write  
access it no longer needs, because nobody has revisited its manifest since the initial  
rollout.

A) This is a Claude Hooks problem — a `PreToolUse` hook should be added to compensate for  
   the plugin's over-broad permissions.
B) This is a plugin-management gap: plugin manifests and their granted capabilities need  
