## Domain 4: Eval, Testing, and Debugging (Q4.1)

### Q4.1 · Debugging and Error Handling
A RAG-backed assistant gives wrong answers on a subset of queries. The team can't yet tell  
whether retrieval is surfacing the wrong documents, whether good documents are being misread  
by the model, or whether the failure is happening in how retrieved content gets assembled  
into the final prompt.

A) Rewrite the system prompt with stronger, more emphatic accuracy instructions, since most  
   RAG failures trace back to insufficiently forceful prompting.
B) Analyze traces of the failing requests — what was retrieved, how the prompt was  
   assembled, and what the model produced from it — to isolate which layer (retrieval,  
   assembly, or model reasoning) the failure actually originates in before changing  
   anything.
C) Upgrade to the largest available model tier immediately, since stronger reasoning  
   capability generally compensates for weaker retrieval.
D) Re-run the same failing queries several times and average the outputs, since  
   inconsistency alone indicates a sampling problem rather than a retrieval or assembly  
   problem.

