## Domain 5: Model Selection and Optimization (Q5.1–Q5.10)

### Q5.1 · LLM Fundamentals
A compliance officer asks for identical, byte-for-byte outputs given identical inputs, and  
an engineer proposes temperature 0 as a full guarantee of this.

A) Correct — temperature 0 makes sampling fully deterministic, so identical inputs always  
   yield byte-identical outputs.
B) Temperature 0 makes generation far more stable and close to deterministic in practice,  
   but the platform does not guarantee bit-identical output across calls; the application  
   should validate against requirements with evals rather than assume exact repetition.
